From: AerynOS packaging
Subject: [PATCH] get_python_lib: use sysconfig instead of distutils

distutils was removed from the standard library in Python 3.12, so this
helper raises ModuleNotFoundError on any current interpreter. cmake runs it
through execute_process and never checks the exit status, so the failure is
silent: PYTHON3_INSTALL_DIR comes back empty, the install DESTINATION becomes
empty, and a build configured with -DENABLE_PYTHON3=ON quietly produces no
bindings at all rather than failing.

sysconfig has been in the standard library since 3.2, and its "platlib" path
is what get_python_lib(plat_specific=True) returned, so this behaves the same
on old and new interpreters. The site-packages fallback below, which decides
the answer whenever the prefix is recognised, is untouched.

--- a/python/get_python_lib.py
+++ b/python/get_python_lib.py
@@ -1,7 +1,12 @@
 import os
 import sys
 import site
-from distutils.sysconfig import get_python_lib
+import sysconfig
+
+def get_python_lib(plat_specific=False, prefix=None):
+    key = "platlib" if plat_specific else "purelib"
+    vars = {"base": prefix, "platbase": prefix} if prefix else {}
+    return sysconfig.get_paths(scheme="posix_prefix", vars=vars)[key]
 
 if __name__ == '__main__':
     prefix = sys.argv[1]
